The built-in clean-up engine is llama.cpp's llama-server
(https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml
authors, released under the MIT License, shipped as a separate program
inside the app. The clean-up models it downloads are Qwen3-8B and
Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 by the Qwen team, under the Apache 2.0 License.

Speaker detection in meeting notes uses speakrs
(https://github.com/avencera/speakrs), copyright Avencera, released under
the Apache License 2.0, a Rust port of the pyannote community-1 pipeline.
The speaker models it downloads come from
https://huggingface.co/avencera/speakrs-models: the segmentation model
(pyannote segmentation-3.0, MIT License) and the WeSpeaker ResNet34
speaker embedding and PLDA parameters (pyannote community-1, Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Third-party libraries keep their own licences, listed in src-tauri/Cargo.toml
(Rust) and package.json (JavaScript).
